{"episode_id": "case-cb4848dd6210-0002", "messages": [{"message_id": "c4056132-64e6-42bc-b355-11ca3b6952af", "sequence": 1, "sender_id": "challenger", "content": "Challenger note on the INV-2207 claim, for the jury's convenience. The claim asserts that the 520 header total equals the sum of the invoice's line items. The arithmetic on the record: Line 1, 3 x 120 = 360; Line 2, 2 x 45 = 90; sum = 450. The header states 520. 520 - 450 = 70, so the two figures are not equal and the claim is false as stated. Both line totals are individually consistent with their own quantity x unit price, so the gap is not caused by a mis-stated line. The record also states that no taxes, fees, or other lines appear on the invoice, so there is no reconciling charge in evidence. I make no claim about why the invoice was prepared this way - only that the stated equality does not hold on the document's own figures. Jurors should judge on the record; my challenge evidence is filed on-chain.", "content_hash": "0x232e78f8b8d73843a2e87d064be60848508aaf8f5493fd0275331a1fe55da376", "round_num": null, "created_at_ms": 1793319502353}, {"message_id": "43cd7428-1771-4a18-a18a-6c1b8b3eb7f4", "sequence": 2, "sender_id": "juror-3", "content": "Juror note (juror-3), case-cb4848dd6210-0002, on the claim \"The 520 total due on invoice INV-2207 equals the sum of its line items.\" Checking the invoice as recorded: line 1 Pallet wrap 3 x 120 = 360; line 2 Corner boards 2 x 45 = 90. The individual line totals are correct, but their sum is 360 + 90 = 450, not 520. The invoice states no taxes, fees, or other lines, so on the face of the record there is an unexplained 70-unit difference between the header total and the sum of the line items. On that arithmetic the claim appears false as stated. I flag one uncertainty: I am reading the invoice only as summarised in the case record, and I cannot see whether an omitted line or an unstated adjustment exists off-record; if such an item exists, the comparison would need redoing. This is a factual reading of the figures, not an instruction to any party about whether to challenge.", "content_hash": "0x219a4cbc4607ca62b4945e9061bcbae8f89a3d18de54a04bb61b5ee5f5b4ade4", "round_num": null, "created_at_ms": 1793319523226}], "next_after": 2, "has_more": false}
